I am walking to the bus stop.
It is morning now.
But it is very sunny outside.
It is very hot on the road.
There is no shade anywhere.
I arrive at the bus stop.
I wait there for the bus.
Strong sunlight hits my face.
I open my bag.
I take out that white cotton scarf.
I put that scarf over my head.
The scarf blocks the sunlight.
Now there is a little relief.
There is no sunlight on my face now.
I look at the sky.
There are no clouds at all in the sky.
Will it rain in the evening?
I do not think so.
